---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';

export const prerender = true;

Astro.locals.locale = 'en';
---

<Legal title="Accessibility statement" updated="August 2026">
  <p>
    Madrid Movilidad was born with the aim that anyone can consult public transport information for the Region
    of Madrid regardless of their abilities, their device or their network conditions. This statement explains
    our level of accessibility and how to notify us of any barrier.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Commitment and level of conformance</h2>
  <p>
    This website has been designed and developed to comply with the W3C <strong>WCAG 2.1, level AA</strong> guidelines, the recognised
    reference in European accessibility regulations. The statement is based on a <strong>self-assessment</strong> carried out by the site
    owner; it has not been audited by an independent third party.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Measures adopted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>“Mobile-first” responsive design: content reflows without being cut off on small screens.</li>
    <li>Full keyboard navigation, with a visible and consistent focus indicator.</li>
    <li>Sufficient text colour contrasts, in both the light and dark themes.</li>
    <li>
      Semantic use of headings, lists, regions and form labels; status messages announced to screen readers.
    </li>
    <li>Decorative icons hidden from assistive technologies; alternative text on informative images.</li>
    <li>Respect for the system’s <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> preference in animations.</li>
    <li>The main searches work without JavaScript (forms with page reload).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Non-accessible content and known limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Interactive maps</strong> (Leaflet with OpenStreetMap tiles): maps have limited textual
      alternatives; the equivalent information (nearby stops, routes and stop listings by direction) is always
      available in text or list format.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Third-party documents:</strong> the linked incident PDFs come from EMT Madrid (in Spanish) and may
      not meet accessibility requirements; their content is summarised in text on the site itself.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Real-time data:</strong> audible alerts and automatic updates may not be available with screen
      readers in all views.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Reporting barriers</h2>
  <p>
    If you encounter any difficulty accessing content or functionality, please write to <a href="mailto:info@madmovil.es">info@madmovil.es</a> indicating
    the page and the problem detected. We will try to provide an accessible response and a reasonable solution as
    soon as possible.
  </p>
</Legal>
